div.p:
Sable, sā′bl, n.  a Siberian species of Marten, with lustrous dark-brown or blackish fur: its fur: a fine paint-brush made of sable: the colour black: (pl.) black clothes, mourning clothes.—adj.  of the colour of the sable's fur: blackish, dark-brown: made of the fur of the sable.—v.t.  to sadden.—adjs.
Sā′ble-stoled;

Sā′ble-vest′ed. [O. Fr. sable—Russ. sabolĭ.]
